From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:01:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] x86/mm: declare pmdp/pudp_test_and_clear_young() only where
 they are defined

arch/x86/mm/pgtable.c defines pmdp_test_and_clear_young() under
CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE || CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_NONLEAF_PMD_YOUNG and
pudp_test_and_clear_young() under CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE, but
asm/pgtable.h declares both unconditionally and sets
__HAVE_ARCH_PMDP_TEST_AND_CLEAR_YOUNG, which hides the generic stub.  On
32-bit x86 (two-level page tables select neither option) the arch thus
declares a function it never defines; clear_refs_pte_range()'s THP branch
references it, dead code that an optimizing compiler removes and a compiler
that keeps it (tinycc, or gcc -O0) turns into an undefined reference.

Put the declarations under the conditions of their definitions so that the
generic stub applies otherwise.  No change for configurations that define
them.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h b/arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h
index d551120a7..91e73f1bc 100644
--- a/arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h
+++ b/arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h
@@ -1302,11 +1302,19 @@ extern int pudp_set_access_flags(struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 				 unsigned long address, pud_t *pudp,
 				 pud_t entry, int dirty);
 
+/*
+ * Defined in pgtable.c under the same conditions; otherwise the generic
+ * pmdp_test_and_clear_young() stub applies (the callers are dead code then).
+ */
+#if defined(CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE) || defined(CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_NONLEAF_PMD_YOUNG)
 #define __HAVE_ARCH_PMDP_TEST_AND_CLEAR_YOUNG
 bool pmdp_test_and_clear_young(struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 		unsigned long addr, pmd_t *pmdp);
+#endif
+#ifdef CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE
 bool pudp_test_and_clear_young(struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 		unsigned long addr, pud_t *pudp);
+#endif
 
 #define __HAVE_ARCH_PMDP_CLEAR_YOUNG_FLUSH
 bool pmdp_clear_flush_young(struct vm_area_struct *vma,
